WEBVTT

00:00:08.150 --> 00:00:10.940
Regarding the Kouki Education 
Academy student's essay,

00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:14.860
it appears to have been an analysis of 
data sent by an unknown sender.

00:00:15.090 --> 00:00:18.740
But that's not something you 
can analyze just like that.

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:22.040
Huh?

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:23.500
What's wrong? You're not on call.

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:26.470
I just remembered I only put it to sleep.

00:00:27.030 --> 00:00:29.880
<i>Someone</i> tends to mess around 
with it without permission.

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:31.990
<i>Want to shut down?</i>

00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:36.250
Why do you have to put everything in folders?

00:00:36.940 --> 00:00:38.220
Well, I'm off for a run.

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:39.760
Hey, wait a minute.

00:00:41.150 --> 00:00:44.850
It's rare to see them having a 
normal conversation like that.

00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:47.810
Not sure I'd call it a conversation. 
More like a lecture.

00:00:47.810 --> 00:00:49.460
I said wait!

00:00:50.270 --> 00:00:52.630
What? If it's about your desktop...

00:00:52.630 --> 00:00:54.490
It's about Kazari Asami.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:57.170
You want to shoot her down that bad?

00:00:57.170 --> 00:00:57.740
Quite the opposite.

00:00:57.740 --> 00:00:58.470
Huh?

00:00:58.730 --> 00:01:00.990
She's an even bigger troublemaker than you,

00:01:00.990 --> 00:01:02.450
but at least she tries.

00:01:03.140 --> 00:01:06.920
I'd like your help in getting her up 
to speed as soon as possible.

00:01:07.510 --> 00:01:09.810
Also, she's a minor.

00:01:09.810 --> 00:01:11.220
We shouldn't bring her when we drink—

00:01:11.220 --> 00:01:12.880
Don't be such a stiff.

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:15.500
Oh! I need to repay you for the last time.

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:19.800
Jeez, you're so like her.

00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:22.200
Both of you lack attention to detail.

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:23.270
Here's the change.

00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:34.610
<i>In response to an increase in heinous crimes,</i>

00:01:34.610 --> 00:01:39.070
<i>a new movement is picking up steam in police 
and security forces around the world.</i>

00:01:40.670 --> 00:01:44.950
<i>This is the story of the services 
performed by ACTIVE in Japan.</i>

00:02:55.690 --> 00:02:58.650
<b>File 4: Holding Airspace</b>

00:03:01.480 --> 00:03:05.180
Ladies and gentlemen, 
we have begun our descent.

00:03:05.180 --> 00:03:08.630
Please return your seats and trays 
to their upright positions,

00:03:08.630 --> 00:03:10.640
and fasten your seatbelts.

00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:12.730
Five minutes behind schedule.

00:03:12.730 --> 00:03:14.800
Sir, we have plenty of time.

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:15.830
Yeah.

00:03:15.830 --> 00:03:18.130
Your daughter may have entered 
the ceremony hall by now.

00:03:18.130 --> 00:03:20.550
She sent me this right before takeoff.

00:03:20.550 --> 00:03:29.850
<b>Dad, do you think you'll make it?</b>

00:03:21.510 --> 00:03:25.780
When I was informed a train derailed today, 
of all days, I was prepared for the worst,

00:03:25.780 --> 00:03:27.920
but thank God there were 
fewer than ten casualties.

00:03:27.920 --> 00:03:29.850
Bigger numbers mean more time.

00:03:29.850 --> 00:03:34.270
I was just hoping we wouldn't get stuck 
in economy for our flight back.

00:03:34.270 --> 00:03:36.440
Ladies and gentlemen, 
this is Manabe, your pilot.

00:03:36.770 --> 00:03:39.280
We were about to begin our approach,

00:03:39.710 --> 00:03:45.410
but we will now enter a holding pattern 
due to a problem at the airport.

00:03:45.760 --> 00:03:48.960
What? But we're almost there...

00:03:48.960 --> 00:03:51.370
My daughter's getting married!

00:03:54.130 --> 00:03:56.240
Defense Minister! What's going on?

00:03:55.360 --> 00:03:56.590
Did North Korea fire a missile?

00:03:56.590 --> 00:03:57.590
Not at all.

00:03:58.010 --> 00:03:59.430
It's nothing.

00:04:04.850 --> 00:04:07.340
Prime Minister, an aerial tanker is ready to go.

00:04:07.340 --> 00:04:08.180
Good.

00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:10.540
But how to interpret this situation?

00:04:10.830 --> 00:04:12.940
Unlike the hijacking six months ago,

00:04:12.940 --> 00:04:16.360
all we have this time is a 
bomb threat on the plane.

00:04:16.360 --> 00:04:20.070
The flight happens to have Dietman 
Gouhara, from Shimane District 3.

00:04:20.070 --> 00:04:21.320
That's beside the point.

00:04:21.810 --> 00:04:23.090
Perhaps it's a malicious prank?

00:04:23.090 --> 00:04:27.680
But the threat was very specific, 
which lends it credibility.

00:04:27.680 --> 00:04:31.000
The bomb was allegedly set in 
Flight 206's main wheel well,

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:33.290
and they even set the holding pattern.

00:04:33.290 --> 00:04:35.150
That's the problem.

00:04:35.150 --> 00:04:39.880
Orochi's "ro" unit is smack in the middle 
of that designated airspace.

00:04:40.200 --> 00:04:43.390
There's a chance that the flight may crash.

00:04:43.390 --> 00:04:44.810
We should evacuate residents.

00:04:44.810 --> 00:04:47.420
But if we don't exercise caution 
in our public statements,

00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:49.350
they'll find out about Orochi...

00:04:52.100 --> 00:04:56.190
<b>There's a plane circling above Kichijouji... A hijacking? 

00:04:54.370 --> 00:04:55.460
Now...

00:04:56.190 --> 00:04:58.180
What will the government's next move be?

00:04:59.150 --> 00:05:01.230
Wow, I'm so excited.

00:05:01.230 --> 00:05:03.080
I want to eat a fruit sandwich.

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:06.120
Yes?

00:05:06.120 --> 00:05:08.110
Sena-kun, are you free right now?

00:05:08.110 --> 00:05:09.040
Yes.

00:05:09.040 --> 00:05:12.290
I successfully purchased a clubhouse sandwich.
Only thirty are made per day.

00:05:12.820 --> 00:05:14.660
I'm heading to Hakkeijima now to try out

00:05:14.660 --> 00:05:16.160
a restaurant famous for soufflé pancakes—

00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:17.870
Sorry! We have an emergency.

00:05:17.870 --> 00:05:18.680
Huh?

00:05:18.990 --> 00:05:21.450
The brass has ordered us to do an EOD.

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:23.050
But...

00:05:23.050 --> 00:05:26.090
You're about to say they should just 
dispatch an EOD squad, right?

00:05:26.090 --> 00:05:27.980
But it's not a dud.

00:05:27.980 --> 00:05:31.310
There was a tip that a plane's 
been rigged with a bomb.

00:05:31.930 --> 00:05:35.860
You're the only one specialized in EOD.

00:05:35.860 --> 00:05:38.840
Also, the flight's in a holding 
pattern above Kichijouji.

00:05:38.840 --> 00:05:41.980
So it's in our own backyard... Roger.

00:05:41.980 --> 00:05:43.280
How's the fuel holding up?

00:05:43.520 --> 00:05:47.270
For now, the United SDF will 
be doing aerial resupply.

00:06:00.680 --> 00:06:02.840
Mobile assault vehicle, linking.

00:06:02.840 --> 00:06:03.840
Linking.

00:06:04.090 --> 00:06:04.840
Linking.

00:06:12.060 --> 00:06:14.330
Hey, what's going on?

00:06:14.330 --> 00:06:16.220
When are we going to land?

00:06:16.220 --> 00:06:18.260
I'm so sorry for the delay.

00:06:18.260 --> 00:06:20.430
We'll land as soon as the 
airport clears us for—

00:06:20.430 --> 00:06:22.560
If Haneda won't clear us, 
why not another airport?

00:06:22.790 --> 00:06:25.360
I'm very sorry. We're exploring 
all available options,

00:06:25.360 --> 00:06:28.280
including landing at a different airport.

00:06:28.590 --> 00:06:29.550
I'm back.

00:06:29.550 --> 00:06:30.370
Sorry again.

00:06:30.370 --> 00:06:32.290
We'll brief you while you suit up.

00:06:32.290 --> 00:06:33.220
Got it.

00:06:33.520 --> 00:06:34.700
I'll go, too.

00:06:35.220 --> 00:06:35.990
Why?

00:06:35.990 --> 00:06:37.930
Well, two's better than one, and all that.

00:06:37.930 --> 00:06:40.120
It'd only distract me, so don't.

00:06:41.810 --> 00:06:45.360
According to the perp's statement,
the bomb was planted

00:06:45.360 --> 00:06:47.570
in Flight 206's main wheel well.

00:06:47.910 --> 00:06:51.300
The bomb will detonate if the 
flight crosses the borders of

00:06:51.300 --> 00:06:52.990
the five wards around Musashino City.

00:06:52.990 --> 00:06:57.270
It will also detonate if the flight's 
altitude falls below 15,000 feet.

00:06:57.270 --> 00:06:59.210
So it can't leave this designated area?

00:06:59.210 --> 00:07:00.630
Seems like it.

00:07:00.630 --> 00:07:02.190
What are they after?

00:07:02.190 --> 00:07:04.280
At the moment, there don't 
seem to be any demands.

00:07:04.580 --> 00:07:08.260
For now, the mobile assault 
vehicle will depart Kichijouji

00:07:08.260 --> 00:07:10.680
and rendezvous with the USDF at Haijima.

00:07:10.680 --> 00:07:11.780
Understood.

00:07:19.590 --> 00:07:21.580
There has been movement.

00:07:27.830 --> 00:07:29.260
Found them.

00:07:29.900 --> 00:07:31.310
They panicked.

00:07:31.310 --> 00:07:34.220
Fools cannot help but let their tongues wag.

00:07:34.590 --> 00:07:37.830
For now, I just want to find the entrance today.

00:07:38.440 --> 00:07:41.870
Will we need Bird's help, as well?

00:07:42.210 --> 00:07:47.770
<b>Haijima</b>

00:07:45.570 --> 00:07:47.770
We apologize for the disruption.

00:07:48.420 --> 00:07:52.110
Although the express train bound 
for Tokyo is scheduled to depart,

00:07:52.110 --> 00:07:56.390
it will leave after the mobile 
assault vehicle passes through.

00:08:02.390 --> 00:08:05.870
Sena-kun, it appears they're ready to refuel.

00:08:05.870 --> 00:08:07.230
Can you go on ahead?

00:08:07.230 --> 00:08:08.090
Got it.

00:08:13.030 --> 00:08:14.260
All right...

00:08:15.220 --> 00:08:16.520
Kuroki-san?

00:08:16.520 --> 00:08:17.790
I'm gonna get ready anyway.

00:08:17.790 --> 00:08:20.840
I think it should be me,
or at least Haruka-san.

00:08:20.840 --> 00:08:22.640
Why do you harass him so much?

00:08:22.870 --> 00:08:23.850
Harass?

00:08:23.850 --> 00:08:26.310
That's right! You're not
letting Sena-san focus—

00:08:26.550 --> 00:08:27.830
That's enough!

00:08:27.830 --> 00:08:29.070
Kuroki-kun, please go.

00:08:29.070 --> 00:08:29.970
Roger!

00:08:29.970 --> 00:08:32.280
Boss? Please explain!

00:08:32.540 --> 00:08:35.910
He's our best at dealing with critical 
situations in emergencies.

00:08:39.770 --> 00:08:41.390
That's Unit 8...

00:08:44.380 --> 00:08:47.970
I'm here from Special Public 
Security Fifth Division,

00:08:47.970 --> 00:08:49.630
Third Mobile Assault Unit 8.

00:08:51.000 --> 00:08:53.710
It's been a while, Garbage Man Sena-kun.

00:08:55.560 --> 00:08:58.430
I'm Ooshikouchi Miho, from the USDF.

00:08:58.430 --> 00:08:59.300
Glad to work with you.

00:08:59.700 --> 00:09:01.670
Er, right...

00:09:02.490 --> 00:09:06.090
Since you're not that surprised, 
I suppose some intel's gone your way.

00:09:06.090 --> 00:09:07.360
Anyway, that's how it is.

00:09:07.360 --> 00:09:09.620
Um, so...

00:09:09.920 --> 00:09:12.780
You want to say, "Why don't you handle it, then?"

00:09:13.080 --> 00:09:14.650
I'd be happy to,

00:09:14.650 --> 00:09:17.410
but the brass ordered us to help with 
refueling and do nothing else.

00:09:18.950 --> 00:09:21.020
Vitals, all green.

00:09:21.020 --> 00:09:21.860
All green.

00:09:21.940 --> 00:09:22.880
All green.

00:09:23.200 --> 00:09:23.700
Lock.

00:09:28.580 --> 00:09:30.710
Inner unit, begin output.

00:09:32.250 --> 00:09:35.880
Oscar II, set strike interceptor unit.

00:09:51.840 --> 00:09:55.320
Oops, we were a second too late...

00:09:55.320 --> 00:09:57.990
I'll go after them. Just launch me!

00:09:58.270 --> 00:09:59.610
Take care.

00:09:59.610 --> 00:10:00.700
We're counting on you.

00:10:09.890 --> 00:10:12.430
All right, time to get to work.

00:10:13.000 --> 00:10:14.320
Cut the crap!

00:10:14.320 --> 00:10:16.010
Why do we keep going around and around?

00:10:16.010 --> 00:10:17.470
What the hell's going on?!

00:10:17.470 --> 00:10:19.760
Sir, please calm down.

00:10:19.760 --> 00:10:21.010
We'll soon be—

00:10:20.270 --> 00:10:21.910
I'm sick of hearing that from you!

00:10:21.910 --> 00:10:23.720
I'm a member of the National Diet.

00:10:23.720 --> 00:10:25.350
I want a proper explanation!

00:10:25.350 --> 00:10:26.690
This is Manabe, your pilot.

00:10:26.990 --> 00:10:29.440
I will now explain our situation.

00:10:29.440 --> 00:10:32.960
Our navigation systems have 
developed a malfunction,

00:10:32.960 --> 00:10:35.460
preventing us from landing safely.

00:10:35.820 --> 00:10:41.000
The USDF is sending a tanker 
to refuel us in mid-air,

00:10:41.000 --> 00:10:44.660
then specialists will repair the system.

00:10:45.380 --> 00:10:47.820
We apologize for the inconvenience,

00:10:47.820 --> 00:10:50.040
but please bear with us for a while longer.

00:10:52.630 --> 00:10:54.460
Oh, the USDF!

00:10:54.700 --> 00:10:57.400
Oh, a plane! A plane!

00:11:00.400 --> 00:11:02.160
We'll get ready on our end, then.

00:11:02.160 --> 00:11:02.970
All right.

00:11:03.270 --> 00:11:06.280
Oscar I, this is just for your information.

00:11:06.280 --> 00:11:07.270
What is it?

00:11:07.270 --> 00:11:09.190
The government has decided not to disclose

00:11:09.190 --> 00:11:11.190
the bomb's existence to the public.

00:11:11.190 --> 00:11:11.900
Huh?

00:11:12.250 --> 00:11:13.310
That's ridiculous.

00:11:13.310 --> 00:11:15.200
If we don't disarm the bomb in time...

00:11:17.860 --> 00:11:19.310
Why would they do that?

00:11:19.310 --> 00:11:22.700
If they don't order an evacuation and 
the worst happens, it'll be a disaster!

00:11:23.380 --> 00:11:24.590
My guess would be...

00:11:24.870 --> 00:11:26.160
Orochi's "ro"?

00:11:27.130 --> 00:11:29.620
The National Public Unified 
Intelligence Matrix?

00:11:29.620 --> 00:11:30.770
Correct.

00:11:31.070 --> 00:11:32.810
The specifics are classified,

00:11:32.810 --> 00:11:36.590
but one of the three split data-modules 
is said to be in Kichijouji.

00:11:36.590 --> 00:11:39.230
Huh? That actually exists?

00:11:39.230 --> 00:11:41.460
The government fears 
the data will be targeted

00:11:41.460 --> 00:11:43.780
if there were a large-scale evacuation?

00:11:43.780 --> 00:11:44.970
Nonsense!

00:11:44.970 --> 00:11:49.680
So as long as the data is safe, they don't 
care what might happen to civilians?

00:11:50.330 --> 00:11:51.390
That's not it.

00:11:52.390 --> 00:11:54.080
There is no "might."

00:11:54.480 --> 00:11:57.720
Failure is not an option in this mission.

00:12:02.320 --> 00:12:03.200
Crap.

00:12:15.250 --> 00:12:17.410
Hey, I'm free after the refueling.

00:12:17.410 --> 00:12:19.560
Can I come watch you work?

00:12:19.560 --> 00:12:21.180
When did you get so malicious?

00:12:21.180 --> 00:12:22.380
What do you mean?

00:12:22.750 --> 00:12:25.830
We can't let anyone else get our data.

00:12:26.920 --> 00:12:29.660
You're pretty loyal for a Unit 8 agent.

00:12:29.660 --> 00:12:30.670
Thanks for noticing.

00:12:30.670 --> 00:12:32.920
You used to be on our side.

00:12:32.920 --> 00:12:34.450
Well, never mind. I'm going ahead.

00:12:44.170 --> 00:12:46.360
HQ, this is Senbu. Starting refuel.

00:12:46.670 --> 00:12:47.740
Start confirmed.

00:12:47.820 --> 00:12:48.830
Start confirmed.

00:12:51.840 --> 00:12:56.250
Kyoukai-san, I've never seen the 
Wears the USDF is using.

00:12:56.250 --> 00:12:58.780
Neither have I. Based on their form,

00:12:58.780 --> 00:13:01.960
I'd say they resemble Iwasaki's 
next-generation prototypes.

00:13:02.220 --> 00:13:05.470
Their stabilizers look pretty damn good.

00:13:05.890 --> 00:13:08.060
Go ahead, garbage man.

00:13:08.650 --> 00:13:11.070
Thank you for the courtesy.

00:13:20.780 --> 00:13:22.890
Command, this is Oscar I.

00:13:22.890 --> 00:13:26.150
I'm going to check if there are any other 
bombs outside the main wheel well.

00:13:30.010 --> 00:13:33.120
Still tiresomely meticulous, I see.

00:13:33.120 --> 00:13:34.660
I'm glad we broke up.

00:13:34.660 --> 00:13:36.580
Stop twisting words around.

00:13:38.040 --> 00:13:40.750
Later, officer!

00:13:40.750 --> 00:13:42.750
Good work.

00:13:43.130 --> 00:13:44.100
Hey.

00:13:44.410 --> 00:13:46.260
This side's more stable.

00:13:46.260 --> 00:13:50.220
I knew you'd follow me, 
you crude scatterbrain!

00:13:50.220 --> 00:13:54.620
They say two's better than one.

00:13:54.920 --> 00:13:58.530
If anything goes wrong, I'll figure it 
out with my big love and courage.

00:13:58.530 --> 00:14:02.370
You're mixing up some song and the Bible.

00:14:02.370 --> 00:14:04.530
Why can't you keep the two separate?

00:14:04.790 --> 00:14:08.670
No one asked you to. You should 
really stop being so nitpicky.

00:14:08.670 --> 00:14:11.210
Whatever. Just stay out of my way.

00:14:11.210 --> 00:14:12.490
Fine, sure.

00:14:12.490 --> 00:14:15.830
Why? I thought he'd tell him to go back.

00:14:15.830 --> 00:14:18.560
Once he shows up, you have no 
choice but to put him to use.

00:14:18.560 --> 00:14:19.960
That's how it is?

00:14:22.380 --> 00:14:23.240
Nothing here?

00:14:23.670 --> 00:14:24.500
Maybe there.

00:14:25.190 --> 00:14:28.950
Sir, I've made arrangements for reaching 
the ceremony hall once we've landed.

00:14:28.950 --> 00:14:29.990
Great!

00:14:29.990 --> 00:14:32.620
I should text my daughter that I'll be there soon!

00:14:32.620 --> 00:14:35.350
Sir, please keep your phone in airplane mode.

00:14:37.860 --> 00:14:41.020
From here on out, can you keep yourself 
out of my field of vision?

00:14:41.020 --> 00:14:41.770
Yeah, yeah.

00:14:51.850 --> 00:14:52.740
Here it is.

00:14:53.000 --> 00:14:55.640
At first glance, it looks pretty orthodox.

00:14:55.640 --> 00:14:59.300
If it had a remote detonator, 
it would've been trickier.

00:14:59.300 --> 00:15:00.920
Talk about a silver lining.

00:15:00.920 --> 00:15:02.960
Maybe it's safe to gear down.

00:15:02.960 --> 00:15:06.350
The change in mass due to refueling 
didn't cause an issue,

00:15:06.350 --> 00:15:08.920
so I'd say you're 98% safe.

00:15:09.640 --> 00:15:11.170
206, do you copy?

00:15:11.470 --> 00:15:12.930
This is 206, copy.

00:15:12.930 --> 00:15:16.070
A police squad will enter the 
right main wheel well.

00:15:16.070 --> 00:15:17.130
Gear down.

00:15:17.130 --> 00:15:19.350
Roger. Gearing down main wheels.

00:15:32.780 --> 00:15:35.490
This looks really old-school.

00:15:37.240 --> 00:15:39.200
I told you to stay out of my field of vision.

00:15:39.200 --> 00:15:41.300
I thought that was for outside.

00:15:41.300 --> 00:15:43.050
I'm saying to give me some space.

00:15:43.050 --> 00:15:46.460
Don't treat me like a stalker! 
The world doesn't revolve around you!

00:15:48.420 --> 00:15:50.940
Kyoukai-san, send over data for S—

00:15:50.940 --> 00:15:53.460
no, PB03 bombs.

00:15:53.460 --> 00:15:54.750
All of it?

00:15:54.750 --> 00:15:57.390
Yeah. I'll sort out the exact type on my end.

00:16:01.180 --> 00:16:02.890
Got one. I think I can handle this.

00:16:08.320 --> 00:16:09.310
What?

00:16:10.430 --> 00:16:11.990
Wh-What is this?!

00:16:12.460 --> 00:16:15.670
Is that Tenten-kun, the guardian mascot 
for warding off fire disasters?

00:16:15.670 --> 00:16:17.300
I'm surprised you knew that.

00:16:17.800 --> 00:16:20.620
Don't worry, that doesn't pose any threat.

00:16:20.620 --> 00:16:22.010
B-But...

00:16:22.330 --> 00:16:23.260
See?

00:16:23.260 --> 00:16:25.290
You can never tell what might happen!

00:16:28.840 --> 00:16:30.080
I see...

00:16:30.080 --> 00:16:32.210
They delayed the start by two hours.

00:16:32.210 --> 00:16:33.930
That should be enough time.

00:16:33.930 --> 00:16:35.270
Well, sir...

00:16:35.270 --> 00:16:35.920
What?

00:16:35.920 --> 00:16:37.610
Due to all the issues,

00:16:37.610 --> 00:16:41.050
the flight's heading to either Second 
Tokorozawa or Yurigaoka Airport.

00:16:41.050 --> 00:16:43.360
So even if they finish the repair right now,

00:16:43.360 --> 00:16:45.350
we'd only arrive at the ceremony hall at—

00:16:45.350 --> 00:16:46.270
What?!

00:16:46.270 --> 00:16:48.440
Damned weasel bastard!

00:16:48.440 --> 00:16:50.910
I wonder what the perp's thinking...

00:16:50.910 --> 00:16:53.770
Maybe he has no intention 
of blowing up the plane,

00:16:53.770 --> 00:16:56.020
given that he put a 
fire guardian mascot there.

00:16:56.020 --> 00:16:57.490
What do you think?

00:16:57.490 --> 00:16:58.780
Who the hell knows?!

00:16:58.780 --> 00:17:01.690
Meteor shower mode, type Jacobini 13!

00:17:10.380 --> 00:17:11.300
All right.

00:17:11.300 --> 00:17:12.840
Just need the password now.

00:17:14.610 --> 00:17:15.260
Whoa!

00:17:16.510 --> 00:17:17.590
You've got to be kidding.

00:17:22.890 --> 00:17:23.890
Oscar I!

00:17:23.890 --> 00:17:26.850
I really wonder what the perp's trying to do.

00:17:41.330 --> 00:17:43.840
Hey, that's Unit 8!

00:17:43.840 --> 00:17:46.290
That's why we're running late!

00:17:46.290 --> 00:17:48.550
See, two's better than one.

00:17:48.550 --> 00:17:50.900
I haven't contested that fact.

00:17:50.900 --> 00:17:52.310
I just don't like you.

00:17:52.310 --> 00:17:53.010
Huh?

00:17:53.350 --> 00:17:57.010
Now isn't the time to turn on me, 
you defense ministry flunky!

00:17:57.010 --> 00:17:57.760
What did you say?

00:17:58.010 --> 00:18:01.810
It's because of people like you that our 
division gets a bad public rap!

00:18:01.810 --> 00:18:03.920
Don't act so high and mighty.

00:18:03.920 --> 00:18:06.960
Even if it's a step down for you, 
for me, it's a way up the ladder.

00:18:06.960 --> 00:18:08.040
You should be happy for me!

00:18:08.040 --> 00:18:10.090
Like hell I can be now!

00:18:11.430 --> 00:18:12.060
Huh?

00:18:12.060 --> 00:18:13.820
Boss, did something happen?

00:18:13.820 --> 00:18:15.370
Hurry, both of you!

00:18:15.370 --> 00:18:17.280
Their second engine's down!

00:18:17.600 --> 00:18:20.740
We may be headed for an emergency landing.

00:18:21.220 --> 00:18:22.630
An emergency landing? But...

00:18:22.950 --> 00:18:25.790
Right. It'll blow if it loses altitude.

00:18:25.790 --> 00:18:26.880
Hurry!

00:18:26.880 --> 00:18:29.500
You just need to enter the 
password to defuse the bomb!

00:18:29.500 --> 00:18:31.000
Fine!

00:18:31.740 --> 00:18:32.960
Wait a minute...

00:18:32.960 --> 00:18:35.270
Stop winging it, seriously!

00:18:41.520 --> 00:18:44.760
Details are the only thing you're 
good with. Keep it together!

00:18:49.810 --> 00:18:52.490
Oscar I, the flight's only 200 
feet from minimum altitude.

00:18:52.770 --> 00:18:53.770
170...

00:18:53.770 --> 00:18:56.070
You scatterbrain, scatterbrain, scatterbrain!

00:18:54.360 --> 00:18:57.690
110... 60... 20...

00:18:56.070 --> 00:18:57.690
Good luck, blockhead!

00:18:57.690 --> 00:18:59.320
They won't make it in time!

00:18:58.680 --> 00:18:59.320
Ten.

00:18:59.320 --> 00:19:00.240
Oscar I!

00:19:00.240 --> 00:19:01.610
Five. Four.

00:19:01.610 --> 00:19:03.830
Three. Two. One.

00:19:01.610 --> 00:19:04.430
Final analysis!

00:19:06.680 --> 00:19:07.760
What happened?

00:19:09.610 --> 00:19:11.960
Good job, blockhead!

00:19:11.960 --> 00:19:13.630
Shut up, scatterbrain.

00:19:14.210 --> 00:19:16.170
Malfunction in right main wheel!

00:19:16.170 --> 00:19:17.000
Huh?

00:19:19.090 --> 00:19:20.470
We'll make a belly landing!

00:19:20.470 --> 00:19:23.320
Lower your heads! Tighten your stomach!

00:19:23.320 --> 00:19:26.450
Brace your legs! Tighten your stomach!

00:19:24.300 --> 00:19:25.760
I'm going to die!

00:19:25.760 --> 00:19:28.270
Who called Unit 8?!

00:19:31.100 --> 00:19:33.960
Paramedic and firefighting backup 
support units in position!

00:19:33.960 --> 00:19:35.440
Start landing mission.

00:19:35.440 --> 00:19:37.400
Please don't! Stop!

00:19:37.660 --> 00:19:39.360
Just do it! I give you full permission!

00:19:39.360 --> 00:19:40.710
Just do it!

00:19:45.440 --> 00:19:47.370
We're maintaining balance?

00:20:02.710 --> 00:20:06.130
How could you sacrifice the units?

00:20:09.020 --> 00:20:10.810
Control tower to firefighting command.

00:20:10.810 --> 00:20:12.520
Report on aircraft's condition.

00:20:12.770 --> 00:20:15.350
Well, it all worked out... With our help.

00:20:15.610 --> 00:20:18.260
But Kyoukai-san's furious.

00:20:18.260 --> 00:20:20.690
Then let's go celebrate without saying hi.

00:20:20.690 --> 00:20:22.140
Let's drink the night away.

00:20:22.140 --> 00:20:23.860
Hey, was it you two?

00:20:23.860 --> 00:20:25.100
Dumbass! Scum!

00:20:25.100 --> 00:20:28.660
I missed a once-in-a-lifetime 
moment because of you two!

00:20:28.660 --> 00:20:29.450
Huh?

00:20:29.450 --> 00:20:31.590
Why was it Unit 8?

00:20:31.590 --> 00:20:34.460
They should've left it to the professionals, 
but you just had to butt in!

00:20:36.170 --> 00:20:38.730
We're professionals, too.

00:20:38.730 --> 00:20:39.840
Y-You bastard...

00:20:41.960 --> 00:20:45.550
So we can't possibly partake in 
the celebratory drinks here.

00:20:45.550 --> 00:20:47.390
We appreciate the thought, though.

00:20:48.760 --> 00:20:50.680
Sir, we can still make it in time.

00:20:50.680 --> 00:20:51.670
Let's hurry.

00:20:51.670 --> 00:20:53.130
Mark my words!

00:20:53.130 --> 00:20:56.270
I had no intention of 
letting the police have that!

00:20:56.550 --> 00:20:57.100
Huh?

00:20:57.100 --> 00:21:00.110
Unbelievable! I will pursue this as an issue!

00:21:00.110 --> 00:21:01.320
A major one!

00:21:01.760 --> 00:21:04.280
Was he talking about Willwears?

00:21:06.800 --> 00:21:07.700
Hey!

00:21:08.910 --> 00:21:11.410
You're the ones who saved us, right?

00:21:11.770 --> 00:21:13.370
This is to thank you.

00:21:15.590 --> 00:21:16.910
Oh, thanks.

00:21:16.910 --> 00:21:17.470
Wait.

00:21:17.940 --> 00:21:20.800
They may construe this as taking a bribe.

00:21:22.780 --> 00:21:25.260
We appreciate the thought.

00:21:27.350 --> 00:21:29.920
Man, you're a real piece of work.

00:21:30.810 --> 00:21:34.600
In the end, we still don't know 
what the perp was after.

00:21:34.600 --> 00:21:36.940
If we only had more freedom,

00:21:36.940 --> 00:21:39.030
we could snoop around more...

00:21:39.420 --> 00:21:41.910
But doing any more would move into politics.

00:21:43.260 --> 00:21:45.500
So we managed to safeguard it?

00:21:45.500 --> 00:21:47.510
Yes, Orochi's "ro" is safe.

00:21:47.510 --> 00:21:49.780
There was no suspicious movement,

00:21:49.780 --> 00:21:52.540
so it must've been a coincidence.

00:21:53.720 --> 00:21:55.260
"To be human

00:21:55.770 --> 00:21:59.460
is to have the freedom to control one's fate."

00:22:00.220 --> 00:22:02.170
Who said those words?

00:22:02.900 --> 00:22:05.630
Marcus Aurelius Antonius?

00:22:05.630 --> 00:22:07.700
Yes, that is correct, Bird.

00:22:07.700 --> 00:22:09.220
Congratulations, Mythos.

00:22:09.220 --> 00:22:13.850
Thanks to the government's bumbling, 
we now know where "O" and "chi" are, as well.

00:22:13.850 --> 00:22:15.220
I must say,

00:22:15.220 --> 00:22:17.990
you are my best partner.

00:22:18.480 --> 00:22:19.780
Thank you.

00:23:50.070 --> 00:23:51.950
<b>Next Episode Preview</b>

00:23:50.700 --> 00:23:51.950
Ohakonyapachininko!

00:23:51.950 --> 00:23:53.230
Welcome to Liko's 
predictions for the future!

00:23:51.950 --> 00:24:04.950
File 5:           Poker Face of Erasure

00:23:53.230 --> 00:23:54.040
What's up next time?

00:23:54.040 --> 00:23:55.050
Huh? What?

00:23:55.050 --> 00:23:57.480
Everyone's drinking, gambling, eating...

00:23:57.480 --> 00:23:59.790
I'm not seeing any signs of serious police work.

00:23:59.790 --> 00:24:01.140
Will they be okay?

00:24:01.140 --> 00:24:03.340
Next time, "Poker Face of Erasure."

00:24:03.340 --> 00:24:05.130
The silence has finally been broken!
